## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical, beginner-friendly design across edge and cloud, data residency, security, and cost—covering IoT Hub, IoT Edge, Functions, SQL with RBAC/RLS, and Power BI, plus BYOK and DR.

## Key Concepts

- IoT Edge integration with IoT Hub
- Edge sampling/filtering
- Serverless enrichment with Functions
- Data partitioning and Row-Level Security in Azure SQL
- BYOK with Key Vault
- Data residency in EU
- DR planning and cost management

## Code Example

```javascript
module.exports = async function (context, eventHubMessages) {
  const enriched = eventHubMessages.map(m => ({
    deviceId: m.properties?.deviceId || m.systemProperties['iothub-connection-device-id'],
    timestamp: m.body?.timestamp || new Date().toISOString(),
    tempC: m.body?.tempC
  }));
  context.log(`Enriched ${enriched.length} messages`);
  // Pseudo: insert into Azure SQL using a managed identity
  return enriched;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate data quality and retention requirements in this pipeline?
- What monitoring would you implement to detect edge preprocessing bottlenecks?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design privacy-preserving ML pipelines across tenants with governance constraints. It also probes how to coordinate training, model registry, and DR while controlling cost.

## Key Concepts
- Federated learning across tenants
- Azure ML orchestration and Delta Lake
- Purview RBAC BYOK governance
- Drift monitoring and auditability
- DR and cost optimization

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for federated training loop
function train_round(tenant_config, local_data_uri, model, aggregator_uri){
  const local_model = train(model, load(local_data_uri));
  const update = compute_update(local_model, model);
  send_update_to_server(aggregator_uri, update);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you detect and respond to drift across tenants?
- How would you handle non-IID data and stragglers in the federation?

## Why This Is Asked
Scenario tests Azure-native, region-conscious design with strict data residency, cross-tenant isolation, and cost control.

## Key Concepts
- Region-bound data planes, tenant isolation, data residency, BYOK, DR, cost levers
- Ingest, processing, and serving layers using Event Hubs, Data Lake, Synapse
- Governance via RBAC, Purview, and Key Vault

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo routing function for tenant-scoped storage
function routeEvent(event){
  const t = event.tenantId;
  // route to tenant partition; security checks omitted for brevity
  return storeInTenantPartition(t, event);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement cross-region read-heavy dashboards while preserving residency?
- What failure scenarios would you test and how would you roll back changes without data loss?
